  "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Image1 is MY OWN spacious animation edit-input master, made only by isolating and arranging MY OWN existing painted action figures. Make a conservative MATERIAL COLOR EDIT ONLY. EXACTLY16 distinct whole-body paintings in the same 4columns x4rows and exact existing order. All existing articulated poses and complete tools/boots must survive unchanged. Keep exact input canvas aspect ratio, all transparent gutters, original subject sizes/positions, camera, anatomy, exposed human faces, hand grips, legs, and original tool geometry including every distinct telescopic extension or breaker angle. Do not enlarge figures into the gutters or cut their feet/tools. Change the fluid INSIDE existing small chemical glass pressure cells on forearms, shoulder/back/spine equipment from muted amber/brown to vivid saturated CHEMICAL GREEN, readable at native HeroesIII scale. Small localized glass highlights only, no green spill/skin or glow clouds. Existing leather straps/cloth may take restrained PLUM/PURPLE accents among worn browns. Keep mechanical piston metal and ordinary armor matte iron/bronze, skin natural. No extra gear or new anatomy. Preserve every independently painted animation action: actual fidget, hit reaction, defensive crouch, direction-changing breaker swing, telescopic-clamp reach, half turn, or non-graphic collapse/corpse as present. Do not substitute idle poses. Do not change layout or invent extra figures. Preserve all whole original silhouettes and alpha edges. Original1999HeroesIII textured painted/prerendered language and upper-left lighting, rough worn cloth/leather/rust, no glossy modern3D/anime. Genuine transparent background, no scenery, painted floor, cast shadows, effects or labels. This is palette consistency repair only, not new action design.",
